<!-- What Is Refurbishment Drylining -->
<h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">What Is Refurbishment Drylining?</h2>
<p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Refurbishment drylining is the process of installing new drylining systems in existing buildings during renovation, conversion, or refitting projects. Unlike new build drylining, refurbishment work involves working in occupied or partially occupied spaces, often with existing walls that need preparation, repair, or complete replacement.</p>
<p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">At <strong>Drylining Edinburgh</strong>, we specialise in drylining refurbishment projects ranging from single-room home renovations to large-scale commercial fit-outs. Edinburgh offers a unique canvas for refurbishment — from Victorian and Georgian tenements across the New Town and Old Town to post-war office blocks in Fountainbridge and Ingliston. Each property type presents distinct challenges that our experienced team is well prepared to handle.</p>

<!-- What We Offer -->
<h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Our Refurbishment Drylining Services</h2>
<ul style="list-style:disc;padding-left:1.5rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;font-size:1.0625rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
  <li>Complete internal wall stripping and replacement</li>
  <li>Upgrading old drylining to modern standards</li>
  <li>New drylining installation over prepared surfaces</li>
  <li>Combined drylining with thermal and acoustic insulation</li>
  <li>Fire-rated drylining upgrades for existing buildings</li>
  <li>Loft conversion and basement conversion drylining</li>
  <li>Office refurbishment and commercial fit-out drylining</li>
  <li>Damp treatment preparation and subsequent drylining</li>
  <li>Tenement flat and townhouse interior refurbishment</li>
  <li>Historic building interior renewal (listed building compliant)</li>
</ul>

<!-- The Refurbishment Process -->
<h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Our Refurbishment Process</h2>
<p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Every refurbishment project is different, but our approach is consistent: we assess, plan, execute, and deliver with professional quality and attention to detail.</p>
<ol style="list-style:decimal;padding-left:1.5rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;font-size:1.0625rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
  <li><strong>Site Assessment:</strong> We visit your property, assess the existing condition, identify any issues (damp, structural movement, outdated insulation), and discuss your requirements and budget.</li>
  <li><strong>Detailed Quotation:</strong> We provide a clear, written quote covering all materials, labour, preparation work, and any additional services such as damp treatment or electrical upgrades. Everything is agreed upfront.</li>
  <li><strong>Site Preparation:</strong> We protect your property, remove old wall coverings if required, treat any damp or structural issues, and prepare all surfaces for new drylining installation.</li>
  <li><strong>Drylining Installation:</strong> Our skilled team installs the new drylining system, including any insulation, fire protection, or acoustic treatments as specified. We work cleanly and efficiently.</li>
  <li><strong>Finishing &amp; Handover:</strong> We complete all taping, jointing, and sanding, conduct a thorough quality check, leave your site clean, and provide documentation for your completed work.</li>
</ol>

<!-- Why Choose Us -->
<h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Why Choose Us for Refurbishment Drylining?</h2>
<ul style="list-style:disc;padding-left:1.5rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;font-size:1.0625rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
  <li><strong>Experience with existing properties:</strong> We understand the challenges of refurbishment work, from working around existing services to dealing with uneven walls and hidden problems behind old coverings. This is particularly valuable for Edinburgh's diverse property stock, from 16th-century tenements to post-war commercial buildings.</li>
  <li><strong>Clean working practices:</strong> We use dust extraction, protective sheeting, and careful scheduling to keep your property as clean as possible throughout the project.</li>
  <li><strong>Flexible scheduling:</strong> We can work around your schedule, including evenings and weekends for commercial clients who need to minimise business disruption.</li>
  <li><strong>Complete solutions:</strong> We can coordinate with other trades (electricians, plumbers, damp specialists) to deliver a complete refurbishment, not just drylining.</li>
  <li><strong>12-month guarantee:</strong> All our refurbishment drylining work is backed by a comprehensive workmanship guarantee for your peace of mind.</li>
  <li><strong>Full documentation:</strong> We provide all necessary certificates, building regulation compliance documentation, and manufacturer guarantees with every project.</li>
</ul>

<!-- Materials & Specifications -->
