<!-- FAQ -->
<h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Frequently Asked Questions about Refurbishment Drylining</h2>
<div>
  <div style="padding:20px;margin-bottom:12px;background:var(--white);border-radius:var(--radius);border:1px solid var(--border);">
    <h3 style="font-size:16px;margin-bottom:8px;color:var(--primary);">What is refurbishment drylining?</h3>
    <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--text-light);margin:0;">Refurbishment drylining involves installing drylining systems in existing buildings during renovation, conversion, or refitting projects. It includes removing old wall coverings, preparing surfaces, and installing new drylining with improved insulation, fire protection, or acoustic performance.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="padding:20px;margin-bottom:12px;background:var(--white);border-radius:var(--radius);border:1px solid var(--border);">
    <h3 style="font-size:16px;margin-bottom:8px;color:var(--primary);">How long does a drylining refurbishment take?</h3>
    <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--text-light);margin:0;">The timeline depends on the project size. A single room takes 2-4 days. Full property refurbishments typically take 1-3 weeks. We provide clear timelines during your quote and work efficiently to minimise disruption.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="padding:20px;margin-bottom:12px;background:var(--white);border-radius:var(--radius);border:1px solid var(--border);">
    <h3 style="font-size:16px;margin-bottom:8px;color:var(--primary);">Can you dryline over existing walls?</h3>
    <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--text-light);margin:0;">Yes. We can install new drylining over existing walls in refurbishment projects, or remove old coverings and install fresh drylining. We assess the condition of existing walls and recommend the best approach for your property.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="padding:20px;margin-bottom:12px;background:var(--white);border-radius:var(--radius);border:1px solid var(--border);">
    <h3 style="font-size:16px;margin-bottom:8px;color:var(--primary);">What improvements can be made during refurbishment?</h3>
    <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--text-light);margin:0;">Refurbishment drylining can add thermal insulation, fire protection, acoustic insulation, and create new room layouts. We often combine drylining with electrical upgrades, insulation, and damp treatment to deliver a complete interior transformation.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="padding:20px;margin-bottom:12px;background:var(--white);border-radius:var(--radius);border:1px solid var(--border);">
